Package: proxywall
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, nftables, systemd, init-system-helpers
Recommends: gir1.2-xapp-1.0 | gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1, ca-certificates, openssh-client
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: @HOMEPAGE@
Description: system-wide proxy client with a kill switch
 ProxyWall sends all traffic of this computer through a SOCKS5 or HTTP
 proxy, an SSH server, or (with Xray installed) a VLESS, VMess, Trojan or
 Shadowsocks server, the way a VPN client would, and keeps a firewall closed around it:
 when the proxy cannot be reached, traffic is blocked instead of going out
 directly.
 .
 It comes with a small desktop interface that shows where your traffic
 comes out (country flag, map and coordinates), a command line tool, an exclusion
 list for domains and addresses that should bypass the proxy (for example
 *.ir or 10.0.0.0/8), DNS leak protection and an always-on mode that also
 blocks traffic after a reboot until the proxy is connected. Chosen
 countries can be blocked as exits: while the proxy comes out in one of
 them, nothing is sent through it.
